WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:02.250
- [Narrator] What do you
get when you put together

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.204
rubber gloves, rain boots, LED lights,

00:00:05.204 --> 00:00:07.121
and a cake saver?

00:00:07.121 --> 00:00:09.947
You get a hitchhiking robot?

00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:11.170
- [Robot] Hello.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:13.590
Would you like to have a conversation?

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.174
(happy symphonic music)

00:00:15.174 --> 00:00:16.888
- [Narrator] Meet Dr. Frauke Zeller,

00:00:16.888 --> 00:00:18.322
and David Harris Smith.

00:00:18.322 --> 00:00:19.315
- Hello.

00:00:19.315 --> 00:00:20.779
- Hello.

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:22.352
- [Narrator] They're the
creators of hitchBOT.

00:00:22.352 --> 00:00:23.495
- [hitchBOT] My name is hitchBOT.

00:00:23.495 --> 00:00:24.723
- [Narrator] Which is?

00:00:24.723 --> 00:00:27.199
- [Dr. Zeller] hitchBOT
is a hitchhiking robot,

00:00:27.199 --> 00:00:29.483
that hitchhikes around the country.

00:00:29.483 --> 00:00:32.316
And is dependent on the help of strangers.

00:00:32.316 --> 00:00:33.608
- [Narrator] So this
DIY robot had a mission.

00:00:33.608 --> 00:00:36.356
To hitchhike across Canada.

00:00:36.356 --> 00:00:38.893
From Halifax all the way to Victoria.

00:00:38.893 --> 00:00:40.742
- [Dr. Zeller] We wanted
people to help the robot

00:00:40.742 --> 00:00:42.844
to really see in the project, how far

00:00:42.844 --> 00:00:44.656
will people go, not just
take a robot in the car,

00:00:44.656 --> 00:00:46.787
but also helping it.

00:00:46.787 --> 00:00:47.620
(white noise)

00:00:47.620 --> 00:00:49.064
- [Narrator] Usually it's
humans who are scared

00:00:49.064 --> 00:00:51.112
that robots will take over the world.

00:00:51.112 --> 00:00:52.045
(crashing of metal)

00:00:52.045 --> 00:00:54.401
(ominous music, screaming and sparking)

00:00:54.401 --> 00:00:56.002
Well, these guys flipped
that idea on its head.

00:00:56.002 --> 00:00:57.728
- [Dr. Zeller] The main question was,

00:00:57.728 --> 00:00:59.118
can robots trust humans?

00:00:59.118 --> 00:01:01.450
- [Narrator] And with
one thumb in the air,

00:01:01.450 --> 00:01:03.655
the international sign
for lemme hitch a ride,

00:01:03.655 --> 00:01:07.059
hitchBOT started its
journey across Canada.

00:01:07.059 --> 00:01:08.537
It quickly captured hearts and minds,

00:01:08.537 --> 00:01:10.226
in Canada and beyond.

00:01:10.226 --> 00:01:11.636
- We heard from many people that they

00:01:11.636 --> 00:01:13.357
would start their day with a cup of coffee

00:01:13.357 --> 00:01:16.328
and opening up the hitchBOT website,

00:01:16.328 --> 00:01:18.884
to see where it had been on the map.

00:01:18.884 --> 00:01:21.695
hitchBOT was getting the
kind of quintessential

00:01:21.695 --> 00:01:25.051
Canadian experience by
heading off for a camping

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:27.449
trip in the Gaspe Peninsula.

00:01:27.449 --> 00:01:29.112
It had ferry rides,

00:01:29.112 --> 00:01:30.878
it went to a First Nations pow wow.

00:01:30.878 --> 00:01:33.131
Really, kind of diverse
cultural experience,

00:01:33.131 --> 00:01:35.132
that really spanned the country.

00:01:35.132 --> 00:01:36.910
- [Narrator] It took
hitchBOT under a month,

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:38.583
and a dozen-and-a-half helpers

00:01:38.583 --> 00:01:41.144
to travel 3800 miles across Canada.

00:01:41.144 --> 00:01:43.466
- I had just recently moved to Canada

00:01:43.466 --> 00:01:45.014
when we started the project.

00:01:45.014 --> 00:01:48.746
I was taken aback by how
helpful and enthusiastic

00:01:48.746 --> 00:01:51.466
they were about this
little robot basically.

00:01:51.466 --> 00:01:53.636
Was wonderful to see the community spirit

00:01:53.636 --> 00:01:55.175
that was built.

00:01:55.175 --> 00:01:56.924
- [Narrator] And that's
the story of how one robot

00:01:56.924 --> 00:01:59.091
hitchhiked across Canada.

